    "id": "10.1016/j.isci.2026.118153",
    "title": "Ion regulatory mechanisms supporting hypersaline tolerance in the coastal rock pool mosquito <i>Aedes togoi</i>.",
    "abstract": "The coastal rock pool mosquito, Aedes togoi, is a remarkable example of a saline-tolerant mosquito. While most mosquitoes are obligate freshwater breeders, Ae. togoi larvae and pupae inhabit coastal rock pools that span freshwater to hypersaline conditions. We explore the ability of Ae. togoi larvae to tolerate hypersaline conditions by profiling the salt gland, an ion regulatory nexus within an anatomically unique, elaborated anal canal. We present a de-novo chromosome-scale genome assembly for Ae. togoi, highlighting its relatively small genome size and differences in chromosomal structure as compared to other Aedine mosquitoes. We detail repeat content and curate key multi-gene families encoding ion-transport proteins enriched in the larval salt gland, building a model of the machinery that likely facilitates hyperosmotic urine formation. Our work provides insights into molecular and anatomical adaptations that underpin the ability of mosquitoes and other insects to thrive in hypersaline rock pools and other dynamic environments.",
    "journal": "iScience",
    "doi": "10.1016/j.isci.2026.118153",
    "date": "2026-11-07",
    "authors": "Chiang J, Khodikian E, Phelan O, Parra AK, Peach DAH, Durant AC, Matthews BJ.",
